{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"curl -fsSL 'https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1002/cne.10323'\"","aggregated_output":"{\"status\":\"ok\",\"message-type\":\"work\",\"message-version\":\"1.0.0\",\"message\":{\"indexed\":{\"date-parts\":[[2026,5,8]],\"date-time\":\"2026-05-08T07:35:37Z\",\"timestamp\":1778225737221,\"version\":\"3.51.4\"},\"reference-count\":62,\"publisher\":\"Wiley\",\"issue\":\"2\",\"license\":[{\"start\":{\"date-parts\":[[2002,8,14]],\"date-time\":\"2002-08-14T00:00:00Z\",\"timestamp\":1029283200000},\"content-version\":\"vor\",\"delay-in-days\":0,\"URL\":\"http:\\/\\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\\/termsAndConditions#vor\"}],\"content-domain\":{\"domain\":[],\"crossmark-restriction\":false},\"short-container-title\":[\"J of Comparative Neurology\"],\"published-print\":{\"date-parts\":[[2002,9,16]]},\"abstract\":\"<jats:title>Abstract<\\/jats:title><jats:p>Five hundred twenty ganglion cells in an isolated whole\\u2010mount preparation of the mouse retina were labeled using the \\u201cDiOlistic\\u201d method (Gan et al. [<jats:ext-link xmlns:xlink=\\\"http:\\/\\/www.w3.org\\/1999\\/xlink\\\" xlink:href=\\\"#bib22\\\">2000<\\/jats:ext-link>] Neuron 27:219\\u2013225) and were classified according to their morphological properties. Tungsten particles coated with a lipophilic dye (DiI) were propelled into the whole\\u2010mount retina using a gene gun. When a dye\\u2010coated particle contacted the cell membrane, the entire cell was labeled. The ganglion cells were classified into four groups based on their soma size, dendritic field size, and pattern and level of stratification. Broadly monostratified cells were classified into three groups: RG<jats:sub>A<\\/jats:sub> cells (large soma, large dendritic field), RG<jats:sub>B<\\/jats:sub> cells (small to medium\\u2010sized soma, small to medium\\u2010sized dendritic field), and RG<jats:sub>C<\\/jats:sub> cells (small to medium\\u2010sized size soma, medium\\u2010sized to large dendritic field). Bistratified cells were classified as RG<jats:sub>D<\\/jats:sub>. This study represents the most complete morphological classification of mouse retinal ganglion cells available to date and provides a foundation for further understanding of the correlation of physiology and morphology and ganglion cell function with genetically manipulated animals. J. Comp. Neurol. 451:115\\u2013126, 2002. \\u00a9 2002 Wiley\\u2010Liss, Inc.<\\/jats:p>\",\"DOI\":\"10.1002\\/cne.10323\",\"type\":\"journal-article\",\"created\":{\"date-parts\":[[2002,9,5]],\"date-time\":\"2002-09-05T20:22:06Z\",\"timestamp\":1031257326000},\"page\":\"115-126\",\"source\":\"Crossref\",\"is-referenced-by-count\":277,\"title\":[\"Large\\u2010scale morphological survey of mouse retinal ganglion cells\"],\"prefix\":\"10.1002\",\"volume\":\"451\",\"author\":[{\"given\":\"Wenzhi\",\"family\":\"Sun\",\"sequence\":\"first\",\"affiliation\":[]},{\"given\":\"Ning\",\"family\":\"Li\",\"sequence\":\"additional\",\"affiliation\":[]},{\"given\":\"Shigang\",\"family\":\"He\",\"sequence\":\"additional\",\"affiliation\":[]}],\"member\":\"311\",\"published-online\":{\"date-parts\":[[2002,8,14]]},\"reference\":[{\"key\":\"e_1_2_7_2_1\",\"doi-asserted-by\":\"publisher\",\"DOI\":\"10.1098\\/rspb.1983.0014\"},{\"key\":\"e_1_2_7_3_1\",\"doi-asserted-by\":\"publisher\",\"DOI\":\"10.1016\\/0006-8993(84)91167-3\"},{\"key\":\"e_1_2_7_4_1\",\"doi-asserted-by\":\"publisher\",\"DOI\":\"10.1002\\/cne.902800108\"},{\"key\":\"e_1_2_7_5_1\",\"doi-asserted-by\":\"crossref\",\"first-page\":\"968\",\"DOI\":\"10.1152\\/jn.1982.48.4.968\",\"article-title\":\"Electrophysiology of retinal ganglion cells in the mouse: a study of a normally pigmented mouse and a congenic hypopigmentation mutant, pearl\",\"volume\":\"48\",\"author\":\"Balkema GW\",\"year\":\"1982\",\"journal-title\":\"J Neurophysiol\"},{\"key\":\"e_1_2_7_6_1\",\"doi-asserted-by\":\"publisher\",\"DOI\":\"10.1523\\/JNEUROSCI.20-2