{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' PR_COMMENTS.md\"","aggregated_output":"This change addresses issue `#3523` by revising `CL_0004117` from the historical label `retinal ganglion cell A` to `alpha retinal ganglion cell` and updating the term so its metadata is internally consistent with the requested concept.\n\nChanges made:\n- Replaced the old minimal text definition with a broader alpha retinal ganglion cell definition supported by `PMID:28753612` (`Krieger et al., 2017`).\n- Added `retinal ganglion cell A` as an exact synonym, sourced to `PMID:12209831`, to preserve the historical name used in the original mouse morphology paper.\n- Added a `term_tracker_item`/issue link back to `https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3523`.\n- Removed the old rat-specific comment, which no longer fit the revised generic alpha RGC concept.\n- Removed the `in taxon Mus musculus` subclass axiom from `CL_0004117`, because the requested relabel and revised definition describe the broader conserved mammalian alpha RGC class rather than a mouse-only class.\n\nRationale:\n- `PMID:12209831` is the source of the legacy `RGA` terminology underlying `retinal ganglion cell A`.\n- `PMID:28753612` explicitly characterizes alpha retinal ganglion cells as a conserved mammalian class with shared morphology, physiology, and four ON/OFF sustained/transient subtypes.\n- Leaving the mouse-only taxon restriction in place would have made the revised label and definition inconsistent with the issue request and with the newer alpha RGC subtype structure already present under `CL_0004117`.\n\nChecks completed:\n- Reviewed the current `CL_0004117` axioms and nearby alpha retinal ganglion subclasses directly in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n- Verified bibliographic metadata for `PMID:28753612` and `PMID:12209831` using Europe PMC/Crossref because the local `aurelian` helper was not installed.\n- Inspected the local diff to confirm that only `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl` changed in the commit.\n\nValidation notes:\n- I could not run `robot convert` or `robot reason` in this environment because `robot` is not installed.\n- I did perform a manual functional-syntax spot check on the edited block after patching.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
